From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 08:10:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: mediatek: keep PDMA IRQ name writable

mtk_get_irqs_pdma() updates the final digit in the IRQ name for each
PDMA ring. The pointer currently refers to a string literal, so kernels
with read-only data protection panic when the function writes rxring[4].

Use a writable local array for the generated IRQ name.

Signed-off-by: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>

---
 drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
@@ -3687,7 +3687,7 @@ static int mtk_get_irqs_fe(struct platform_device *pdev, struct mtk_eth *eth)
 
 static int mtk_get_irqs_pdma(struct platform_device *pdev, struct mtk_eth *eth)
 {
-	char *rxring = "pdma0";
+	char rxring[] = "pdma0";
 	int i;
 
 	for (i = 0; i < MTK_PDMA_IRQ_NUM; i++) {
-- 
2.47.2
